// A loop that fills EVERY element is a whole-initialisation, so a later read is sound.
// `for k in 0..8 { a[k] = 7 }` writes every slot, but definite-init is a MUST analysis over a
// per-element lattice and the store is at a SYMBOLIC index, so it learned nothing and `a[7]`
// afterwards was [E005] — an over-rejection of an entirely ordinary idiom. The comprehension
// form already states the fact with IR_INIT; a fill loop is the same fact written differently.
//
// Measured by scripts/fuzz/fuzz_init.sh as the ONLY over-strict shape it could produce
// (8 of 8 in a 60-program run), which is what named the idiom instead of leaving a vague
// sense that the pass was strict. The refusing side is pinned by loop_fill_partial_fail.ln.
func main() i32 {
    var a i32[8]
    for k in 0..8 { a[k] = 7 }
    return a[7] - 7
}
